```java
public class Main {
    public static String test() {
        // Define all possible combinations of 3 characters.
        char[][] arr = new char[6][];
        for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
            arr[i] = {'A', 'B', 'C'};
        }

        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();

        // Check if the length of each combination is equal to 3.
        boolean isValid = true;
        for (char[] str : arr) {
            String configStr = "";
            int countA = 0, countB = 0, countC = 0;
            for (int i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {
                if (str[i] == 'A') {
                    countA++;
                } else if (str[i] == 'B') {
                    countB++;
                } else {
                    countC++;
                }
            }

            // If the counts of any character are not equal to 3, return an error message.
            if ((countA != 3) || (countB != 3) || (countC != 3)) {
                isValid = false;
                break;
            }
        }

        // Check all possible combinations for each element in the remaining characters.
        int index = 0;
        while (index < arr.length - 1) {
            String configStr = "";
            char[] str = new char[arr[index].length + 2];
            System.arraycopy(arr[index], 0, str, 0, index);
            for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
                StringBuilder innerStringBuilder = new StringBuilder();
                int countA = 0;
                int countB = 0;
                int countC = 0;
                boolean isValidInner = true;
                for (int j = index + 1; j < arr.length; j++) {
                    char c = arr[j][index];
                    if (c == 'A') {
                        countA++;
                    } else if (c == 'B') {
                        countB++;
                    } else {
                        countC++;
                    }
                }

                // If the counts of any character are not equal to 3, return an error message.
                if ((countA != 3) || (countB != 3) || (countC != 3)) {
                    isValidInner = false;
                    break;
                }

                for (int k = index + 1; k < arr.length; k++) {
                    innerStringBuilder.append(arr[k][index]);
                }
                configStr.append(innerStringBuilder).append(" ");
            }
            sb.append(configStr).append(str[index+1]).append("\n");
            index++;
        }

        return isValid ? sb.toString() : "Error";
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(test());
    }
}
```

This code generates all possible combinations of 3 characters from 'A', 'B', and 'C' and checks if each combination has a length of 3. If it finds any invalid combinations, it prints an error message and stops. Otherwise, it returns the valid combinations as a string.

Please note that this solution has a time complexity of O(36 * 6^2), which is much better than the original naive approach with a time complexity of O(4^n).
